# sriq ABox split (slice 9j): abox-fold-type-clash's control. B ⊑ ∀r.D instead, so a's types agree.
# ∃r.C ⊑ E makes A ⊑ E, which the hierarchy run reads with the ABox gone.
# Expect: consistent; A ⊑ E.
@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .

:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class . :E a owl:Class . :r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :C ] .
:B rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:allValuesFrom :D ] .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :C ] rdfs:subClassOf :E .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual , :A , :B .
